=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported symptom — VLAN-10 hosts (172.16.10.x, switch1/pc5–pc8) being unable to reach VLAN-30 hosts (172.16.30.x, switch3/pc12–pc14) via the multilayer core switch mswitch0 — does not exist in the live network. Eight independent ping tests were executed covering every VLAN-30 destination from multiple VLAN-10 sources (pc5→pc12, pc5→pc13, pc5→pc14, pc6→pc12, pc7→pc12, pc8→pc14), plus cross-checks from mswitch0 itself toward both VLANs. All returned 0% packet loss with sub-2 ms RTT.

The inter-VLAN routing infrastructure is fully healthy: mswitch0 has correctly configured VLAN SVI interfaces (vlan10@br0 172.16.10.254/24, vlan20@br0 172.16.20.254/24, vlan30@br0 172.16.30.254/24, all UP), end-hosts point to those SVIs as their default gateways, and FRR OSPF on mswitch0 advertises all three VLAN prefixes into the wider network. The downstream access switches also check out — switch1's br_vlan10 bridge and switch3's br_vlan30 bridge are both UP with the correct port membership. No iptables rules exist on mswitch0. VLAN-10 to VLAN-20 cross-VLAN reachability was also verified clean. The ticket describes a fault condition that is not present in this topology; the network is operating normally.

Root cause: The helpdesk ticket is a false alarm — no network fault exists between VLAN 10 and VLAN 30. No corrective action is needed.
=== END ===